Rationale for this change
A ref created with a retention policy (max ref age, max snapshot age and minimum snapshots to keep) loses all three settings once a branch is written to, or once main is moved with set_current_snapshot or rollback_to_snapshot. The ref is rebuilt without them, so the policy a table owner set is silently unset.
Fast-forward already carries the settings over. This change makes branch writes, set_current_snapshot and rollback_to_snapshot do the same, and a ref created without a policy still stays unset. It continues #3770 and is separate from #3760, which expires stale refs.
Are these changes tested?
Yes, with a live reproducer; the commands and observed output are under Testing Done.
Testing Done
The reproducer below uses the public API against a SQLite-backed catalog with a local warehouse. It creates a branch with a policy, writes to it three times, then rolls main back and forward again, printing the policy after each step. A branch created without a policy is the control. The same script runs twice on one checkout: first with the one changed source file taken from origin/main, then with the branch's own file.
Before, with the file from origin/main:
$ git checkout origin/main -- pyiceberg/table/update/snapshot.py
$ uv run --frozen --extra pyarrow python repro_ref_retention.py
branch created        : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
after 3 branch writes : {'max_ref_age_ms': None, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': None, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': None}
main with a policy    : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
after rollback        : {'max_ref_age_ms': None, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': None, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': None}
after set_current     : {'max_ref_age_ms': None, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': None, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': None}
branch with no policy : {'max_ref_age_ms': None, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': None, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': None}
After, with this branch's file:
$ git checkout HEAD -- pyiceberg/table/update/snapshot.py
$ uv run --frozen --extra pyarrow python repro_ref_retention.py
branch created        : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
after 3 branch writes : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
main with a policy    : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
after rollback        : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
after set_current     : {'max_ref_age_ms': 86400000, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': 3600000, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': 5}
branch with no policy : {'max_ref_age_ms': None, 'max_snapshot_age_ms': None, 'min_snapshots_to_keep': None}
Only the SQLite-backed SqlCatalog on a local filesystem was exercised.
Reproducer source: repro_ref_retention.py
